{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1429958-question-about-baal-caress-quietus-4-masquerade-20th","id":1429958,"title":"Question about Baal Caress (Quietus 4), Masquerade 20th","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-26T10:05:21-08:00","id":1429958,"title":"Question about Baal Caress (Quietus 4), Masquerade 20th","content":"Hi everyone<br /> <br /> First of all sorry about my english.<br /> <br /> I have a question about Quietus 4, Baal caress. In the book does not say what happend when you dont use transmuted points of blood in a weapon. I just want to know how much last these transmuted points. I checked google for an answer before asking here but I only found one post about this on reddit, they said that is up to the storyteller but it should not last more than a scene. However my storyteller says that these points are eternal and the effect last untill the end of times. But I think that this is wrong since if its like that another vampires could kidnap and dominate an assamite to milk these points from him.<br /> <br /> So what do you think guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26610-kastis","name":"kastis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T11:08:01-08:00","id":1429961,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure unused points are lost at the end of scene and become inert or just dissolve into nothingness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T13:56:06-08:00","id":1430494,"title":"","content":"Come on guys I need more replies on this. I want to know your opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26610-kastis","name":"kastis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T14:32:50-08:00","id":1430499,"title":"","content":"Quietus isn't the best written discipline.<br /> <br /> RAW, it seems like it could be indefinite, and at the end there's &quot;For this reason, many vampires choose to coat their weapons with a significant quantity of blood&quot; suggesting they stockpile it. This also makes it quite comparable to 'Burning blade&quot;, a level 2 ritual, which also lasts until it's used rather than a period of time.<br /> <br /> Alternatively looking at the book, I think Quietus poisons, as products of vitae, last just as long as vitae does outside the body. If it is permanent, perhaps the -it's still kinda vitae- thing keeps Assamites from stockpiling the poison en-mass, because thaumaturges could take advantage of the poison.<br /> <br /> A lot of powers end with 'till the next sunrise' if that's more your boat.<br /> <br /> You could also look at the storyteller's vault for more comprehensive Quietus rules on a pay-what-you-want scheme... eh... Why do I feel guilt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 12-30-2020, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count